Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:36.550
Good morning. Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.980
Kashino, are you okay?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.830
Ah, it's people from Team Ichigo.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.870
Who are you guys?

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:55.330
Pleased to meet you. We're Team Lemon who will be competing against our senpais in the quarterfinals.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.320
We respect our senpais a lot.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.840
In the first round, to make such a splendid rose pound cake. It's amazing.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.520
It's such an honor to be able to compete with our senpais. It's just like a dream come true.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.890
Please take care of us.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.800
Please.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.870
I see, so they're just a bunch of good kids.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.580
Same to you. Just because you're a first year, we aren't gonna hold back.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.540
Let's have a fair battle.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.540
Yes!

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.490
Lessons are starting! We have to go!

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:42.710
recipe 20

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:42.710
Formidable Enemy<i>!</i> ? A Transfer Student From Paris

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.050
Formidable Enemy!? A Transfer Student From Paris.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:48.550
The first years in Team Lemon. They were a bunch of honest and cute kids.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.430
Are you blind?

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.800
Didn't you feel any malicious intent behind the smiles of theirs?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.980
I felt it too.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.480
I have a feeling that they despise us.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:03.650
I wonder about that...

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:08.410
You two are thinking too much. Our opponents are first-years after all.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.750
Naïve!

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.090
I-It's nothing...

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.170
Kashino and Hanabusa-kun are saying that?

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.100
They're definitely thinking too much...

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.580
Oh yeah, know your enemy and the battle will be a breeze.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.160
But, how can I know more about them?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.470
Wanna check them out tomorrow?

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.140
There they are.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.470
Morino-kun's father is the chef of a famous French restaurant in Tokyo...

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:44.570
...while his mother is a pâtissière.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:49.580
Ayashi-kun has mixed blood of a Japanese and Belgian, where chocolates originated from.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.260
Kujou-kun's family owns an established Japanese confectionery house in Kyoto.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.750
The young master of the Kinjon family that won the national Japanese confectionery competition.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:02.480
Their years are top-notch. And they're always ranked top 3 amongst the first years.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.630
It feels that they are a replication of the Sweets Princes, don't they?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.330
Okay, what about Lemon-chan?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:12.420
She is a transfer student who recently transferred from the main campus of St. Marie Academy in Paris.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.380
I don't really know but they are a formidable group.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.200
She's totally different from me.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:28.610
Nice shot. You're pretty good, aren't you.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.430
Kyoto's Kujou, you say?

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:43.670
Nevertheless, I heard they have a renown Japanese confectionery house and are continuous winners of the annual whatchamacallit.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.690
I know about them. It can't be, that Kujou's son is a member of that team...

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.560
When making a cake, the name of the house or background doesn't matter.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.880
But he's from the Kujou's-

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.060
It doesn't matter!

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.860
I agree with Kashino.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.860
If we act as normal, they won't be an opponent we can't defeat.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.210
But, well... Getting to know about our opponents isn't a bad thing to do.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:17.420
Oh, I have friends in the school's TV broadcasting club.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:21.330
I will go and borrow the DVD recording of their last battle.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.260
Amazing! They look as if they are the Sweets Princes.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.790
They made really small pound cakes, huh?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.110
I wonder what they're going to do.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:57.790
A-Amazing! They made a family of geese.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.830
It totally fits a family's theme.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.330
They got full marks for all 3 segments.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:11.010
I never would have thought that they had this kind of potential.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.760
They aren't just any ordinary first-years.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.260
In the first round, to make such a splendid rose pound cake. It's amazing.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.810
To have Kashino and Hanabusa-kun be so agitated by it...

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:29.110
Such a meticulous Maccha Pound Cake...

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:32.010
...as expected of Kujou's son.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.310
Come on, guys. It's true that they're amazing,

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:41.290
but we got praised for our Pound Cake by the Chairman didn't we?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:45.070
But in terms of skills, we lost to them.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.290
If we compete against them in the first round, what would happen?

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.190
You don't have to sweat that.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:56.800
In the quarterfinals, we'll use a different kind of cake.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.930
We just have to win with that.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:04.170
That's right. Now that we know the potential of our opponent, we just have to take extra care.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:05.100
That's right, that's right!

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.120
All right! Let's do our best!

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:13.360
W-What! Everyone has to encourage themselves or it won't work.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.430
Aren't you the one who needs to work hard the most!?

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.740
Oh. That's right...

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.610
Speaking of Kujou of Kyoto, it's the best amongst the established names.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:42.540
On a different level than my family's Yumetsuki.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:50.640
Today is the quarterfinals yet I didn't get any sleep at all.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.030
Andou-kun. You woke up pretty early.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.130
Ah, Chairman. Good morning.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.630
Morning.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:01.940
Are you fishing?

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:05.000
My hobby is fly-fishing.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.580
I can get a good catch early in the morning.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.320
A hit!

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:17.230
Is that a rainbow trout?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.470
No, it's a red salmon.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:25.680
Please grow older and become the guardian spirit of this lake.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.100
Chairman. I have a question to ask you about.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.400
What is it?

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.480
I would like to request you to tell me the theme for today's quarterfinals.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:42.100
The four members of Team Lemon already came to ask me.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:46.430
I told them, "It's classified until the match."

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:47.650
I see.

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:52.250
What's the matter? Sweets Princes who are always brimming of confidence.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.080
That's not the case!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.380
Please excuse me.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:17.250
We will now commence the Cake Grand Prix quarterfinals.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:21.020
So then, Chairman. Please explain the match rules.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:30.460
The confrontation this time isn't a team match. The winner will be decided through individual matches.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.080
Individual competition?

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:42.020
After discussing with the teachers, we concluded that everyone has to make four kinds of sweets, being one a cake.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.510
The first kind is cupcake.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:46.260
I'll do that one.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.560
The second one is fudge chocolate.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.710
I will take that.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.570
The third is fruits jelly.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.620
Ah! I made those before at my house.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.600
Then, it's decided Ichigo-chan will take that.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:00.370
The fourth one is something of my liking.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:05.480
Please make a Japanese confection that kindles the coming of spring.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.990
That will be... mine.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.510
Seems I made it in time.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:28.380
With that, we'll start the quarterfinals first round.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.500
Team Ichigo.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.930
The opponents are... Team Lemon.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:37.630
You're late.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.950
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.190
Hey, look, look. Tennouji-senpai is here too.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:49.180
For the the high school grand champion Tennouji-senpai to come here and see the round...

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.310
Ichigo-chan and the others must be amazing.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:55.490
It isn't just for Team Ichigo. Team Lemon is also of her interest.

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:56.180
Eh?

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.000
Team members, please stand at your positions.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.520
Commence cooking.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:18.430
Senpai. Since we are going to compete anyway, why don't we use the same ingredients?

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.570
That's true. It's going to difficult to compete if there are too many choices.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:25.150
My name is Ichigo, so I want to make a strawberry one.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:28.210
That sounds good. After that, how about complementing with that orange?

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:28.870
Sure.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:33.050
I like kiwi, so I want to use kiwi.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:34.120
Kiwi?

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:38.180
I've never used kiwi in jelly before...

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.880
But, since Lemon-chan likes it, it's fine.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.590
Thank you very much.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.920
It's fine, it's fine.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:52.250
He's using dough added with butter, huh.

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:56.770
Interesting. Since we are going to compete, I should use the same ingredients too.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.490
Lemon-chan... What is she boiling?

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:15.040
As I expected, Kujou's son will be making an arrangement based on the Sakura of Arashiyama.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.180
So you're planning on making kinton, senpai?

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:21.710
By the way, I heard that you are the son of a Japanese confectionery house.

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:24.070
Do you know my family's house?

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:24.910
Not at all.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:27.220
Then, why do you ask?

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.210
My family's house is an established name.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:33.300
The whole nation's Japanese confectioneries are just imitations of my family's house's snacks.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.710
Same with your family's house.

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.410
Don't say such rude things.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.170
We've made this kinton for generations in my family!

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.910
Eh, that doesn't matter though.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.270
That guy...

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.680
No... I'm getting dizzy because of my lack of sleep.

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.370
What's wrong? You look pale.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:58.080
Don't worry. I'm just a little dizzy.

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.440
No, it's nothing.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:02.920
I'm just talking to myself.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:19.700
Senpai, are you okay?

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.120
Your face looks pale.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:21.640
It's nothing!

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.650
Andou-kun, what's wrong?

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:26.520
No, it's nothing.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.020
The roses are more beautiful than usual.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.370
Beautiful.

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:44.280
Yeah. It's just like Satsuki, flawless.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:47.910
Magical macaron, Sweets Romance Card.

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.330
Come out!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:57.110
Kashino-senpai. I'm about to finish making my sweets.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.320
Kashino, are you okay? Time's almost up.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.060
Okay.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:21.160
The one beside has already started to decorate.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:25.000
Here too. Afterwards, I just have to add in the meat floss and it will be okay.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.640
Kashino is taking longer than usual today, huh?

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:37.380
He's a perfectionist, so there's no need to be worried.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.680
That's right.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:39.720
Andou is...

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.450
Magical macaron, Sweets Romance Card.

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:48.980
Come out!

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:51.430
Sakura and oil flower, is it?

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.260
Both represents spring.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:54.610
It's difficult to declare the winner, isn't it?

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.700
Ichigo-senpai?

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:58.780
Why have you been muttering to yourself since just now?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.490
Ah, no, that's...

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.390
I forgot that she can't see Vanilla.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.570
I have a bad habit of talking to myself from time to time.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:10.770
Senpai, it's about time the jelly is solidified, isn't it?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.850
T-That's right, let's take them out.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.550
It is solidified pretty well.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.070
Eh? You are using a donut mould?

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:23.890
I made mine based on the image of a jewel.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.630
Huh?

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:30.900
Oh no, it can't be!

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.860
So then, let's begin grading.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:41.750
Let's see what shall we start from first...

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.300
The winner has already been decided for the fruit jelly before tasting.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.500
Yamagaishi, what do you mean?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:53.160
I completed mine, but Ichigo-senpai's...

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.510
You..!

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.230
I'm sorry.

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:09.010
I don't know what went wrong, but the gelatin didn't solidify...

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:11.770
That was because you used unboiled kiwi in it.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:12.630
Eh?

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:16.990
There are enzymes in kiwi that will dissolve proteins.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.820
When you use it, the gelatin will be digested.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.410
S-So that's why Lemon-chan was boiling it.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:31.060
Yamaguchi-san, back then I was looking at you both when you were selecting the ingredients.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:36.290
You purposely chose kiwi because you knew that Amano-san didn't know about them.

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:38.160
Yes, yes. I saw it.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:41.050
Oh? Is that so?

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.010
Stop it, Andou.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:48.220
Amano is the one at fault for not making even the basics.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:52.040
Besides, I already figured that she would lose.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:55.570
No way...

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.530
I guess we don't have to taste them.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:04.450
If they want to enter the semifinals, they can't lose any points for the next two.

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:11.750
Both pass their baking skills and taste.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.880
But we have to make a decision.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:23.090
Why?! When you said that both of us passed!

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:29.650
True, we can't find a deciding factor, but there is a great difference in the decorations.

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.810
The rose that Hanabusa made is first-class.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:34.520
Yay~!

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:43.200
This battle is really difficult to conclude.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.240
The deciding factor is the cocoa's design.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.130
Yay!

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.300
As expected of you.

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:55.500
Andou, if you win, we will be able to enter the semifinals.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.570
I'm counting on you.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.670
Y-Yeah.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:03.830
The champions of the national Japanese confectionery competition for the past 5 years,

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.140
I have made an arrangement of the Sakura of Arashiyama from my father's house, Kujou.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:12.770
And I too have made an arrangement of my family's house original Yumetsuki's Rape Blossom Kinton.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:17.970
Oh, both of them gives a good feeling of the coming spring.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.060
Then, I will start with the Arashiyama Sakura.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.400
Splendid.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:35.540
The image of Kyoto's Arashiyama with the sakura in full bloom appeared before me!

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.040
This is...

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.740
...definitely not like Andou.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.620
He miscalculated the amount of refined white sugar.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:54.660
At that time...

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.140
I also think it's too sweet.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:05.740
I... lost...

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:09.620
No way...

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:11.640
This makes it a draw.

